From: Ashraf Bashir <eng.bashir@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Add frontlight warm/cold percentage indicators to status
 bar

Pin a warm/cold frontlight percentage readout to the top-left corner,
drawn on every screen (reader and non-reader) that already renders the
top status bar clock.

frontlightWarmth is stored as 0 (cool) .. 100 (warm); the cold reading
shown is its complement (100 - warmth) rather than a separate setting.
It has a default (50) and is loaded at boot, so there is always a value
to display from the first frame.

Placement: hooked into drawTopStatusBarClock() rather than drawHeader(),
because drawHeader() is not actually called on every screen - MinimalTheme
and RoundedRaffTheme both override it with their own implementations, and
the reader's status bar (drawStatusBar, at the bottom of the screen while
reading) is a separate function again. drawTopStatusBarClock() is the one
function called from all three header variants and from every reader
activity (Epub/Txt/Xtc), so it is the only place that is truly universal.
The new draw call is placed ahead of the clock's own visibility checks so
it renders even when the clock itself is hidden or the RTC is unavailable.
Positioning is computed independently of the clock's centered text and the
battery's own layout, so neither is touched.

Icons are drawn with drawLine/fillRect only, since GfxRenderer has no
circle primitive; the sun is a filled square core with four rays, the
snowflake is three crossed lines.

